{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 10, 16]], "date-time": "2026-10-16T21:52:01Z", "timestamp": 1792187521385, "version": "4.4.0"}, "reference-count": 207, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "28", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 28]], "date-time": "2024-05-28T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1716854400000}, "content-version": "am", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/"}, {"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 28]], "date-time": "2024-05-28T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1716854400000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/"}], "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/501100000923", "name": "Australian Research Council", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["DE220101354,DP240102891"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["DE220101354,DP240102891"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100000923", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["Advanced Materials"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2024, 7]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Vanadium redox flow batteries (VRFB) are a promising technology for large\u2010scale storage of electrical energy, combining safety, high capacity, ease of scalability, and prolonged durability; features which have triggered their early commercial implementation. Furthering the deployment of VRFB technologies requires addressing challenges associated to a pivotal component: the membrane. Examples include vanadium crossover, insufficient conductivity, escalated costs, and sustainability concerns related to the widespread adoption of perfluoroalkyl\u2010based membranes, e.g., perfluorosulfonic acid (PFSA). Herein, recent advances in high\u2010performance and sustainable membranes for VRFB, offering insights into prospective research directions to overcome these challenges, are reviewed. The analysis reveals the disparities and trade\u2010offs between performance advances enabled by PFSA membranes and composites, and the lack of sustainability in their final applications. The potential of PFSA\u2010free membranes and present strategies to enhance their performance are discussed. This study delves into vital membrane parameters to enhance battery performance, suggesting protocols and design strategies to achieve high\u2010performance and sustainable VRFB membranes.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1002/adma.202402090", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 22]], "date-time": "2024-05-22T11:44:05Z", "timestamp": 1716378245000}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 118, "title": ["The Critical Analysis of Membranes toward Sustainable and Efficient Vanadium Redox Flow Batteries"], "prefix": "10.1002", "volume": "36", "author": [{"given": "Jiaye", "family": "Ye", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "School of Chemistry and Physics Faculty of Science Queensland University of Technology  Brisbane QLD 4001 Australia"}, {"name": "Centre for Materials Science Queensland University of Technology  Brisbane QLD 4001 Australia"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Lu", "family": "Xia", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "ICFO\u2010Institut de Ci\u00e8ncies Fot\u00f2niques The Barcelona Institute of Science and Technology  Castelldefels Barcelona 08860 Spain"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Huiyun", "family": "Li", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Center for Automotive Electronics Shenzhen Institute of Advanced Technology Chinese Academy of Sciences  Shenzhen 518055 China"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "F. Pelayo Garc\u00eda", "family": "de Arquer", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "ICFO\u2010Institut